<metadata>
  <!--
    Binding fixes for OpenTracing API (io.opentracing:opentracing-api)

    OpenTracing is a transitive dependency from the Datadog Android SDK. The MAUI plugin
    does NOT expose any OpenTracing types to users - it provides a custom ISpan interface
    for complete abstraction.

    Analysis shows:
    - NO public APIs expose OpenTracing types
    - Android implementation uses reflection to access native Datadog tracer
    - iOS uses OpenTelemetry (not OpenTracing)
    - The only OpenTracing import (IO.Opentracing.Propagation) is in disabled code that
      throws NotImplementedException due to binding conflicts

    Conclusion: Safe to exclude the entire io.opentracing package to avoid binding issues
    with generics (Tag<T>), circular dependencies (Span/Scope/Tracer), and nullability.
  -->

  <!-- Remove the entire io.opentracing package - not used by MAUI plugin public APIs -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[starts-with(@name, 'io.opentracing')]" />
</metadata>
